tasks.brief:
Rewrite src/api/chat.py: Import stream_reply from src.services.llm. Define FastAPI APIRouter. Define POST /api/v1/chat endpoint accepting ChatRequest body (message: str). Call stream_reply(request.message) and wrap in StreamingResponse with media_type='text/event-stream'. For each ("token", content) chunk, write SSE frame: 'event: token
data: {"content": "<content>"}

'. For ("done",) chunk, write SSE frame: 'event: done
data: {}

'. For ("error",) chunk, write SSE frame: 'event: error
data: {"message": "<FALLBACK_REPLY>"}

'. Ensure exactly one terminal event (done or error) is emitted per request, always last. No exceptions escape the route handler; all failures are framed as SSE error events. Acceptance: POST /api/v1/chat with {"message": "test"} returns 200 with StreamingResponse; token chunks yield event: token frames in order; done yields event: done after tokens; error yields event: error with FALLBACK_REPLY message on failure or empty completion; missing message returns 422 before handler runs.
